<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Copi raises interim shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Copi raises interim shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million Canadian dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)		95	 vs     78</p>
<p>    Net earnings	    16.77	 vs     13.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   18.72	 vs     14.64</p>
<p>Tax</p>
<p>    - current		  1.95	 vs     1.34</p>
<p>    - deferred		  nil	 vs     0.32</p>
<p>Interest paid</p>
<p>    - current		  1.00	 vs     1.44</p>
<p>    - long-term		0.35	 vs     0.47</p>
<p>    Sales		     86.28	 vs     90.17</p>
<p>Full name: Canadian Overseas Packaging Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said current levels of demand and prices for the Corporation's products were expected to continue during the second half. It said, however, the length of the buoyant conditions on many major stock exchanges suggested that the current level of investment performance may not be sustained in the next half.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
